\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Gauge transfer operators at finite volume}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{A positive character expansion turns a temporal plaquette weight
into a positive operator on spatial link fields. Multiplication by
half of the spatial weight on each side gives a transfer operator.
Gauge averaging selects its physical states and retains the temporal
links when the time direction closes into a circle.}

\p{The construction uses a finite spatial graph, normalized Haar
measure and the [positive kernel hypotheses](fdip-007I). It proves
finite periodic-time trace identities, a spectral Hamiltonian and
link-reflected positivity for bounded spatial observables. The
[Gaussian transfer construction](fdip-007S) supplies the scalar
comparison; [reflection positivity by itself](fdip-007Q) does not
supply these operator and translation data. The time direction
and the transfer powers are Euclidean. The spectral Hamiltonian
also generates unitary real-time evolution on the same physical
Hilbert space; [[fdip-00N4]] relates it to vacuum correlations.
No Euclidean geometric algebra is identified with a Lorentzian one.
Normalized Haar measure uses
compactness of the gauge group. \ref{fdip-00LY} records that
#{SL(2,\mathbb R)} has no such probability.}

